== ui_card "Flash Helper"
  p.sp-text-muted <code>ui_flash(type, message)</code>

  h3 Philosophy
  p Flash messages provide ephemeral feedback to the user. The `ui_flash` helper integrates with a Stimulus controller to:
  ul
    li Automatically animate the entry of the message.
    li Provide different visual indications for success vs. danger.
    li Handle accessibility roles (alert).

  h3 Arguments
  == ui_table ["Name", "Type", "Description"],
    [["type", "Symbol", "The nature of the message: <code>:notice</code> (neutral/success), <code>:alert</code> (danger)."],
     ["message", "String", "The text content to display."]]

  h3 Real World Scenarios

  h4 1. Success Message
  p Triggered after a successful action.
  .sp-card
    .sp-card__body
      == ui_flash :notice, "Changes saved successfully."
      == ui_code '== ui_flash :notice, "Changes saved successfully."'

  h4 2. Error Alert
  p Use when something goes wrong.
  .sp-card
    .sp-card__body
      == ui_flash :alert, "Failed to connect to database."
      == ui_code '== ui_flash :alert, "Failed to connect to database."'

  h3 Live Demo
  p Click to trigger a toast (simulates a flash message):
  button.sp-btn.sp-btn--primary onclick="window.showToast('Hello World', 'notice')" Trigger Toast
